Subject: [PATCH] Limit an oversized hopper stack after a fast path insert, as
 Paper's setItem does

A stack above its item's maximum (made with /data merge or /item replace) was left at count-1 by the fast path but is cut to
the maximum by Paper's push. Found with the differential test using commands.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/level/block/entity/HopperBlockEntity.java b/net/minecraft/world/level/block/entity/HopperBlockEntity.java
index 277219bf18d654079ee86a76f60988af49cd8c59..cfd03c13aef01a411713d8c63395e0071e400306 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/level/block/entity/HopperBlockEntity.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/level/block/entity/HopperBlockEntity.java
@@ -1564,6 +1564,8 @@ public class HopperBlockEntity extends RandomizableContainerBlockEntity implemen
                 if (!transferStack.isEmpty()) {
                     boolean transferSuccess = net.caffeinemc.mods.lithium.common.hopper.HopperHelper.tryMoveSingleItem(insertInventory, transferStack, fromDirection);
                     if (transferSuccess) {
+                        // Paper stores the remainder with setItem, which limits an oversized stack (made with commands or NBT) to its maximum
+                        transferStack.limitSize(hopperBlockEntity.getMaxStackSize(transferStack));
                         if (insertInventoryWasEmptyHopperNotDisabled) {
                             HopperBlockEntity receivingHopper = (HopperBlockEntity) insertInventory;
                             int k = world.spigotConfig.hopperTransfer; // Spigot
